<TextLayout title="Proof privacy policy" description="How Proof handles your photographs, projects, and optional purchases.">
  <p>Last updated November 5, 2026.</p>
  <p>Proof lets you create contact sheets from photographs you choose to import. Your projects, imported copies, annotations, and drawings are stored on your device. Proof does not upload these files to a developer-operated server. Your device&#x27;s backup settings may include app data in backups managed by Apple.</p>
  <p>Proof accesses images you select through Apple&#x27;s Photos and Files interfaces. It uses imported copies and does not modify your originals. When you export or share a sheet, you choose its destination. The receiving app or service handles that shared file under its own privacy policy.</p>
  <p>Proof does not include advertising or analytics tracking, and does not require an account.</p>
  <p>Optional one-time support purchases use Apple&#x27;s App Store payment system. Apple processes payment information. Proof receives StoreKit product and transaction information to complete purchases and does not receive your card details.</p>
  <p>If you contact support, the developer receives the information you choose to include in your message and uses it to respond. Avoid sending private photographs or sensitive information unless needed for your request.</p>
  <p>You can remove projects within Proof. Removing the app removes its local app data, subject to Apple&#x27;s backup and device-management behavior.</p>
  <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:support@schneider.kim">support@schneider.kim</a>.</p>
</TextLayout>
